Thanks Joe. Shiny is developing into such a useful piece of my toolkit, making it super simple to turn any of my analysis into an interactive app. In some cases, I think it aids exploratory analysis as well. For example, see this app on visualizing the Reinhart-Rogoff debt study.

http://glimmer.rstudio.com/ramnathv/rChartsRogoff/

The first slider shows what happens to the averages if you change the cutting point from 90, a simple way to graphically determine if there is a tipping point, as proposed by their paper. So, I believe Shiny is going to be a very useful tool for research, in addition to showcasing it as an app.

Best,
Ramnath

